WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.261
Remember when people couldn't stop talking
about Duck Dynasty's Robertson family? A few

00:00:05.261 --> 00:00:10.870
short years ago, this close-knit Louisiana
clan was the talk of reality TV, but everything

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:16.510
changed after Phil Robertson's notorious GQ
interview in 2013. The Robertsons managed

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:20.950
to stay on the air following their brush with
controversy, but lost a vast portion of their

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:25.280
audience, and were dropped from A&amp;E in March
of 2017.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.940
"Well, hey! There ain't nothin' I can do about
that now, we done screwed the pooch here!"

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.860
Did the Robertsons just disappear after that?
Not by a long shot. So, where are they now?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.470
Phil &amp; Kay Robertson

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:41.110
In an interview with local news station KNOE
8, Phil and Kay Robertson said they don't

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:45.330
have any grand plans for the future. Phil
said he's basically going to spend all day

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.841
in the woods, while Kay is looking forward
to getting back to a "quieter life." Phil

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.770
wasn't sad to see them pack their cameras
and go.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:01:00.760
"I, for one, was thankful it ended. There's
a lot more to doing these TV shows than most

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.030
people realize."

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.540
While the Robertson family patriarch would
like everyone to think he's happy checking

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.259
duck blinds all day, he's actually been pretty
busy outside the Louisiana wilderness. During

00:01:10.259 --> 00:01:15.359
the 2016 U.S. Presidential Election, Phil
became politically active, voicing his support

00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:19.789
for Republican candidate Ted Cruz before switching
to supporting Donald Trump, and he's been

00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:24.030
quietly playing behind the scenes in conservative
politics ever since.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.150
Phil and Kay also travel around doing speaking
engagements, mainly preaching their religious

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.000
beliefs in what Phil described as, quote,
"helping our neighbors and living a godly

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.890
life." Recently, he's taken to Facebook to
advocate for the NRA, which should surprise

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:38.649
exactly no one.

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:44.509
"My idea of happiness is killing things. Boom
bom bombombombomb bow."

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:46.659
Willie &amp; Korie Robertson

00:01:46.659 --> 00:01:50.960
The Duck Commander himself, Willie Robertson,
also took a deep dive into politics as the

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.429
show tapered down, speaking at the Republican
National Convention in 2016. Willie attended

00:01:56.429 --> 00:02:01.709
the 2017 Presidential inauguration and even
visited the White House. Lately, he's hinted

00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:06.149
at possible new TV projects and discussed
an expansion of the family's West Monroe,

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:07.149
Louisiana warehouse.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:10.260
"I'm fixin' to go crazy redneck up in here!"

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:15.250
But like his dad, Willie's also not resting
on his laurels. He and his wife Korie decided

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.920
to reopen Willie's Duck Diner, a local family-themed
restaurant once featured on the show. Along

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.840
with his partner in the restaurant, Willie
was also instrumental in organizing relief

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.940
efforts for victims of Hurricane Harvey.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:30.200
Meanwhile, Korie has parlayed her TV fame
into a brand of her own. Already a New York

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.730
Times bestselling author, Korie released her
latest book post-Duck Dynasty, called Strong

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:39.140
and Kind: Raising Kids of Character, which
she paired with her Strong + Kind collection

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.750
of housewares, jewelry, and accessories.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.500
But there's one area where she and Willie
differ. In a surprising break from the family,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:50.910
Korie told CNN that she didn't share her husband's
enthusiasm about Donald Trump, and stated

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:55.230
that her and her husband agree to disagree.
She also called on the president to, quote,

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.500
"be a leader that unifies, that brings people
together."

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.040
Sadie Robertson

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.410
Arguably the breakout star of the show, Willie
and Korie's daughter Sadie has become a full-blown

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:10.350
media figure in her own right since the final
duck call, starting in 2014, when she nearly

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:14.510
took home the mirrorball trophy on Dancing
With The Stars. Since then, she's also become

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.490
a bestselling author, launched clothing lines,
and started an acting career.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.600
Just like her mother, Sadie's taken the concept
for her book, Live Original, and turned it

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.690
into a full-blown brand, which includes a
blog and live show. Sadie views herself as

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:31.240
"a beacon of light in an oft-dark world,"
and she's working on a follow-up book, Live

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:34.870
Fearless, which she says is about her "journey
of finding freedom."

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.010
John Luke Robertson

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:42.170
The second oldest child of Willie and Korie,
John Luke also got a jumpstart on his post-Dynasty

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:47.560
career. In 2014, he authored a series of children's
books called Be Your Own Duck Commander before

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:52.400
venturing into non-fiction with Young and
Beardless: The Search for God, Purpose, and

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.510
a Meaningful Life, a memoir about camp, volleyball,
and anguish over things like his girlfriend

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.680
getting texts from other guys.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.701
Taking a cue from his family, John Luke also
seems to be building a personal brand. He's

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:07.261
launched a blog called Young &amp; Beardless,
as well as promoted the handle through his

00:04:07.261 --> 00:04:11.380
social media accounts, although a quick look
at recent posts suggests he may already have

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:15.630
to consider re-branding to Young &amp; Scruffy.
And if that doesn't work out, he clearly has

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.289
a future in endorsing canned fish.

00:04:18.289 --> 00:04:22.610
"Bumblebee tuna. Bumblebee tuna. Bumblebee
tuna."

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.910
Uncle Si Robertson

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:29.490
"I'm like a bat. Kaboom! Kapow! Punch! Zap!
Kick!'

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:34.050
As the last season of Duck Dynasty was airing,
Uncle Si launched his A &amp; E spinoff series

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:38.330
Going Si-ral, which pitted the quirky technophobe
against the world wide web.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:45.610
"I got myself a show about the internet. I'm
not even sure what that is, yet."

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:50.789
He's also busy working on new music and about
to start touring with his band, Uncle Si &amp; The

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:55.160
Sicotics, which is comprised of himself, his
daughter-in-law Marsha Robertson, and Bridgette

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.160
Tatum.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.639
Si must have learned a thing or two from his
solo series, because he and his bandmates

00:04:59.639 --> 00:05:04.550
now routinely post lengthy Facebook Live posts
that keep fans engaged, but also play out

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.740
like a reality show. And if you just can't
get enough Si, they're also selling ringtones.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:18.849
"It's ringin', ringin', ringin'! Hey, Jack!
Answer the phone!"

00:05:18.849 --> 00:05:23.180
At any rate, it looks like diehard Uncle Si
fans are still able to get their fill of the

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:27.900
eccentric Vietnam vet, and for that we say
God bless the internet, Jack!

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.960
"Hey ya! Oh! Woah!"

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.260
Jase &amp; Missy Robertson

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.319
Though there was already a huge internet kerfuffle
when photos of the pre-beard Robertson clan

00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:43.800
surfaced online, it happened all over again
in September 2017 when Jase Robertson lost

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.650
a battle with the buzzer for a great cause.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:51.259
Jase agreed to shave as part of a fundraiser
for Mia Moo, the foundation he and his wife

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:52.779
Missy founded, which is

00:05:52.779 --> 00:05:57.169
"...dedicated to raising awareness and funds
towards research, treatments, and causes of

00:05:57.169 --> 00:05:58.909
cleft lip &amp; palate."

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:02.879
Jase and Missy were moved to start the foundation
after the outpouring of support they received

00:06:02.879 --> 00:06:07.320
when their own daughter, Mia, was born with
the condition. The goal for #ShaveJase was

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.999
to raise $100,000 dollars, after which Jase
would shave and cut his hair and record it

00:06:11.999 --> 00:06:15.849
live. Though they missed their goal, Jase
honored his pledge, and posted the video to

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:19.949
Facebook via his new venture, CamoFlix, which
Jase described as

00:06:19.949 --> 00:06:25.199
"...a place where outdoors people, hunters,
fisherman, fisherwoman can go and share videos."

00:06:25.199 --> 00:06:30.199
Think of it like YouTube, only you need a
fishing license or a hunting tag to upload.

00:06:30.199 --> 00:06:34.719
A few days after Duck Dynasty's final episode
aired, Missy Robertson told the Daily Journal,

00:06:34.719 --> 00:06:39.029
"Right now, we're taking some time off to
rest and re-evaluate what our next steps will

00:06:39.029 --> 00:06:41.330
be…"
"I'm enjoying being able to travel to see

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:45.129
[my sons] Reed and Cole, who are currently
living in Nashville and Malibu, and spending

00:06:45.129 --> 00:06:47.509
time with Mia and all her activities."

00:06:47.509 --> 00:06:51.360
Missy has yet to strike out on a completely
new venture, but she's continued her work

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:55.729
with her jewelry line, Laminin, which focuses
on pieces which are, quote, "made by women

00:06:55.729 --> 00:07:00.539
who have come out of very difficult situations."
Laminin has become more than just a jewelry

00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:02.979
retailer—it's also an outreach program.

00:07:02.979 --> 00:07:08.400
"All women can come together who would like
a job, who need a job, and that can express

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.529
their creativity, and just being a part of
each others' lives."

00:07:11.529 --> 00:07:15.749
Through the creation of the Laminin House,
Missy hopes to expand across the United States,

00:07:15.749 --> 00:07:19.159
and serve as a ministry to disadvantaged women.

00:07:19.159 --> 00:07:20.969
Reed Robertson

00:07:20.969 --> 00:07:24.599
Still in Nashville and plugging away at his
fledgling country music career, Reed Robertson

00:07:24.599 --> 00:07:29.240
recently released his new EP, although he's
still pretty far from the big time. He told

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.240
The Outdoor Experience,

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.870
"We didn't have a plan, and we didn't really
have a defined sound that we were going for.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:38.729
We just got in the studio and had fun and
just wrote, and it just kind of happened,

00:07:38.729 --> 00:07:39.729
which is really cool."

00:07:39.729 --> 00:07:44.499
Reed was married to Brighton Thompson in October
2016, and the newlyweds have been posting

00:07:44.499 --> 00:07:48.449
happily-ever-after Instagram shots ever since.

00:07:48.449 --> 00:07:50.339
Jep and Jessica Robertson

00:07:50.339 --> 00:07:54.559
Knowing a good thing when they saw it, A &amp; E
greenlit a spinoff for Jep Robertson and his

00:07:54.559 --> 00:07:59.569
wife Jessica before Duck Dynasty ended. But
like every other Robertson, Jep and Jess couldn't

00:07:59.569 --> 00:08:04.309
possibly have just one iron in the fire, which
is why in addition to operating Jess's jewelry

00:08:04.309 --> 00:08:09.949
line, Cavalry, the couple also launched a
podcast, The Jep &amp; Jess Show, in March 2017.

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:13.689
The busy couple said the show would be even
more revealing than before, and would definitely

00:08:13.689 --> 00:08:18.069
feature regular visits from the rest of the
Robertson family. So in case you were worried,

00:08:18.069 --> 00:08:21.169
yes, all the charm of the reality show is
still intact.

00:08:21.169 --> 00:08:25.900
"By the time I'm through, y'all are gonna
pee in your pants, and then you're gonna throw

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:26.460
up."

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.120
Yep, charming.

00:08:28.569 --> 00:08:31.540
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.719
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

